# Two binary packages from the one wheel (split-service spec §3.24, PR-3.7).
# collins-service is the headless half and installs on a box with no
# display: the whole Python package (one tree, so the window's modules ride
# along as files the service never imports), the collins-service and
# collins-keeper commands, and both systemd user units, never enabled or
# started by the package. collins is the window: its launcher, desktop
# entry, icons and metainfo, and the GTK stack. It depends on the
# collins-service built from the same source, since the window's own
# modules are in it. debian/*.install say which file goes where.
Package: collins-service
Architecture: all
# What the service and the keeper import, and no more:
# tests/test_service_imports.py holds them to GLib, GObject and Gio (which
# gir1.2-glib-2.0 carries) and api/server.py's libsoup 3; the service
# imports no markdown library. bubblewrap is Recommends: it is what a
# sandboxed session's box is built with, and without it Collins says so in
# Preferences and launches every session unsandboxed, which is what it did
# before the feature existed. bindfs and fuse3 (fusermount3) are Recommends
# too: with them a directory allowed to a sandboxed session reaches it while
# it runs; without either the grant applies at the session's next restart,
# and Preferences says so. All three run on the service's side, so they are
# this package's (apt installs a dependency's Recommends with collins too).
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-glib-2.0,
         gir1.2-soup-3.0
Recommends: bubblewrap,
            bindfs,
            fuse3
Description: headless session service for Collins
 The half of Collins that runs Claude Code sessions: collins-service holds
 every session's terminal, its sandbox and the repository and pull request
 calls, and collins-keeper keeps the terminals alive across a service
 restart. Both come with systemd user units the package never enables.
 Installed alone, it is the service on a headless box that a Collins
 window on another machine reaches over ssh.

Package: collins
Architecture: all
# The two versioned floors are the ones measured against actual API use:
# Gtk.FileDialog and Gtk.FontDialog are GTK 4.10, and Adw.AlertDialog,
# Adw.Dialog, Adw.PreferencesDialog and Adw.AboutDialog are libadwaita 1.5.
# Without them a too-old stack installs cleanly and then dies at import, which
# matters because this package is also the only channel Debian has.
# gtksourceview5 and vte are deliberately unversioned: nothing has
# established what their real minimum is, and a guessed floor locks out
# users who would have been fine. libspelling is only Recommends: the
# composer degrades to an unchecked text box without it. So is GStreamer
# (the core typelib and the base plugins, which carry playbin): it plays the
# notification sound, and without it the display's beep does.
# python3-markdown-it and python3-linkify-it (pure Python, Architecture: all
# preserved) render pull request bodies as real markdown blocks; without
# them the PR page falls back to a plainer regex renderer, but rich PR
# rendering isn't optional in spirit, so they are Depends, not Recommends.
# The window reaches its service over libsoup 3 as well
# (collins/api/client.py), so gir1.2-soup-3.0 is named here too.
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         collins-service (= ${source:Version}),
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.10),
         gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5),
         gir1.2-vte-3.91,
         gir1.2-gtksource-5,
         gir1.2-glib-2.0,
         gir1.2-soup-3.0,
         python3-markdown-it,
         python3-linkify-it
Recommends: gir1.2-spelling-1,
            gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0,
            gir1.2-gst-plugins-base-1.0
Description: native GTK4 desktop app to manage Claude Code sessions
 Collins browses every Claude Code session on your machine in a
 sidebar grouped by project, lets you name and star them, and resumes any of
 them in embedded terminal tabs.
 .
 It is an unofficial community tool, not affiliated with Anthropic, and never
 modifies the agents' own session data.
